clos.loDetails:
Understand sentence structures, test format (General or Academic), different kinds of exercises at intermediate level in IELTS tests
+ Listening: identify types of information to fill in the blank, recognize common traps and vocabulary relating to different topics: names, address, and phone number;
+ Reading: know how to approach different question types - True, False, Not Given, Multiple choice, Matching headings, how words are paraphrased and how to quickly analyze a sentence/ paragraph;
+ Writing: analyze the topic, identify key words, develop ideas and know how to write an essay (types and questions);
+ Speaking: know how to make an outline and give complete answers in Speaking sections
